  "narrative": "Synthesis resolves the pending PTEN MSI-exclusion line and the KEAP1 media-serum interaction validation deadline. For H121, PTEN loss within the TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-wildtype and MSI-stable context is strongly replicated: discovery R115 is +0.260 [0.182, 0.339] and independent validation R119 is +0.300 [0.180, 0.420], both wholly above the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed stronger-dependency direction. I therefore accept and close H121. This supports the conclusion that the accepted conditional PTEN-loss association is not merely an artifact of overlap with the much stronger MSI-high association, although it remains a conditional supplied-dataset association rather than a broad PTEN claim. For H92, the reversed KEAP1-loss media-serum interaction was threshold-level in discovery, R72 +0.173 [0.044, 0.303], but independent validation R93 was only +0.057 [-0.124, 0.238]. Validation does not refute the discovery finding, but it is not threshold-level and is consistent with a much smaller attenuation. I therefore leave H92 unresolved and close it. The main KEAP1-loss weaker-dependency effect remains accepted in both high-serum and low-serum direct strata; the evidence for a meaningful high-serum attenuation is not stable. Overall supported supplied-dataset conclusions are: TP53 loss is associated with higher, i.e. weaker, composite dependency (replicated, H13/R1+R26); KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker dependency (replicated, H3/R3+R13); SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger, i.e. more negative, composite dependency (replicated, H4/R4+R39); MSI-high is associated with stronger dependency (replicated, H111/R105+R106); and PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency specifically in the TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-wildtype background, with replication after excluding MSI-high (H67/R54+R66 and H121/R115+R119). These associations are robust across many direct context strata for the core predictors, including subtype, ploidy, culture, and serum conditions, though not every individual interaction was confirmatory. Negative or unsupported findings include the constructed research markers, STK11, MTAP, KRAS, ARID1A, ERBB2, MYC, PIK3CA, RB1, APC, SMAD4, BRCA2, NF1, BRAF, EGFR amplification in adenocarcinoma, Avana/Ky/Humagne-CD library main effects in the tested directions, and multiple rejected serum, lineage, Cas9, growth-rate, culture, and stemness interaction modifiers. Remaining unresolved uncertainty includes full-population PTEN, CDKN2A-loss overall and in MTAP or ploidy contexts, full-population EGFR amplification, and the KEAP1 high-serum attenuation line now closed as unresolved. The most informative next work would be broad technical-quality and demographic screening using safe binary variables, such as matched-omics availability, to assess residual measurement confounding, while avoiding further reopening of already well-supported core associations. All conclusions are associations within the supplied dataset and do not establish causality or external biological generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 9 synthesis: H121 accepted and closed; validation confirms PTEN-loss association in TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-wildtype background after excluding MSI-high, so MSI overlap is not the primary driver of that conditional PTEN line. H92 remains unresolved and closed: discovery suggested high serum attenuates KEAP1-loss weaker-dependency association by about 0.17 units, but validation point estimate was only about 0.06 with interval crossing threshold; direct KEAP1 main effects remain accepted. Current accepted core supplied-dataset associations: TP53-loss -> weaker composite dependency; KEAP1-loss -> weaker dependency; SMARCA4-loss -> stronger dependency; MSI-high -> stronger dependency; PTEN-loss -> stronger dependency only in TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-wildtype background and replicated excluding MSI-high. Remaining low-priority unresolved lines: full PTEN, CDKN2A overall/MTAP/ploidy contexts, full EGFR, KEAP1 serum interaction. Future next analysis could register only broad binary technical-quality screens such as has_matched_rna_dna or related omics-availability flags; these are artifact screens, not new biological claims."
}
